&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>This course covers the mathematical underpinnings of reliable software, using the &lt;em>Software Foundations&lt;/em> textbook series, now available as an interactive online book with executable 
&lt;a href="https://leanprover.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lean&lt;/a> code embedded directly in the text. Students learn functional programming, logic, and how to construct machine-checked proofs about programs.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>See the 
&lt;a href="https://www.engineering.upenn.edu/~cis5000/current/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course website&lt;/a> for the syllabus, schedule, and other details.&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>